{"recordFormat":"standalone-informed-source-inventory-candidate-v1","recordId":"chemie-current439-HB-primary232-informed-independent-b-20261017-v1.clause-021","runId":"chemie-current439-HB-primary232-informed-independent-b-20261017-v1","sourceGoalId":"hb-chemistry-sekii-gyo2022-clause-p09-std-e-standard-e1-e12-gk_lk-04","sourceClauseIds":["HB2022-p09-STD-E-standard-E1-E12-GK_LK-04"],"verdict":"revise","scope":"Exact clause body plus its provenance/operator/course/topic record, as inactive source inventory only; no canonical credit","findingId":"HB232-B-01","frozenScientificReasoning":"### HB232-B-01 — E4 purpose/scope — REVISE\n\nSourceGoal `hb-chemistry-sekii-gyo2022-clause-p09-std-e-standard-e1-e12-gk_lk-04`; clause `HB2022-p09-STD-E-standard-E1-E12-GK_LK-04`; physical/printed page9, E4.\n\nThe current sourceText/parentBulletText/title/description read as planning investigations **including hypothesis testing**. The original E4 plans experimental or model-based approaches, with variable control where appropriate, **also** for testing hypotheses, statements or theories. It does not make hypothesis testing the sole specified purpose of all such planning. The current operator list `planen` does not restore the omitted objects or the original additive qualification. Restore the breadth and the 'auch' relationship, including statements and theories; do not turn every investigation plan into mandatory hypothesis testing or require every task to test all three categories. The current conditional treatment of variable control is otherwise sound. Update the corresponding page9 authored passage when revising this body.\n","physicalPage":9,"currentCourseLevel":"GK_LK","currentSourceScope":{"officialTopicStatus":"cross_topic_standard","selectionRule":null,"selectedByLearner":null,"universalOfficialRequirement":true},"requiredOperators":["planen"],"scientificViewPin":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-HB-primary232-neutral-scientific-review-preparation-ro