{"recordFormat":"standalone-informed-source-inventory-candidate-v1","recordId":"chemie-current439-HB-primary232-informed-independent-b-20261017-v1.clause-055","runId":"chemie-current439-HB-primary232-informed-independent-b-20261017-v1","sourceGoalId":"hb-chemistry-sekii-gyo2022-clause-p12-std-b-standard-b2-b14-gk_lk-12","sourceClauseIds":["HB2022-p12-STD-B-standard-B2-B14-GK_LK-12"],"verdict":"revise","scope":"Exact clause body plus its provenance/operator/course/topic record, as inactive source inventory only; no canonical credit","findingId":"HB232-B-03","frozenScientificReasoning":"### HB232-B-03 — B13 assessment objects — REVISE\n\nSourceGoal `hb-chemistry-sekii-gyo2022-clause-p12-std-b-standard-b2-b14-gk_lk-12`; clause `HB2022-p12-STD-B-standard-B2-B14-GK_LK-12`; physical/printed page12, B13.\n\nThe current paraphrase names consequences of chemical products, methods and one's own actions. The original B13 additionally explicitly names **Verfahren** and **Erkenntnisse**, alongside products and methods, while retaining one's own actions and ecological/economic/social sustainability perspectives. The current B12 row does retain all four chemical objects, so the omission in B13 cannot be dismissed as a consistent umbrella terminology policy. Its operator metadata lists only assessment verbs and does not restore the missing objects. Restore procedures/processes and knowledge/findings in B13's source body and corresponding page12 passage. Both original assessment operators, the three sustainability perspectives and own action are already preserved.\n","physicalPage":12,"currentCourseLevel":"GK_LK","currentSourceScope":{"officialTopicStatus":"cross_topic_standard","selectionRule":null,"selectedByLearner":null,"universalOfficialRequirement":true},"requiredOperators":["beurteilen","bewerten"],"scientificViewPin":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-HB-primary232-neutral-scientific-review-preparation-root-v1/REVIEW.HB-current232-whole-source-clauses-t